Both remaining failures are projection-width errors, not filter/join errors: sp0362 returned all 4 columns of `Paragraphs` where gold projects one attribute column (`Other_Details`, all NULL), and sp0755 returned only the base table's 15 columns where gold projects every column of both joined tables (19). The current rule ("whole entity -> SELECT T1.*") guesses width from surface wording. Prior attempts at this diagnosis were dropped for bundling an unrelated text-matching tweak; this candidate changes only the projection rules plus a tightly-scoped shape check in solve.py that re-asks about projection width using execution evidence (all-NULL columns / star over fewer tables than joined).

